It is Friday afternoon, and I am off from work.
I walk down the street and stop at a florist.
I intend to buy a gift for Eva.
I open the door and walk into the small shop.
"Good afternoon," the clerk says with a big smile.
"Good afternoon," I reply.
I look at the many beautiful flowers.
I think that Eva always likes colours.
She is a designer, so she will probably love something colourful.
I find a large bouquet with yellow tulips.
"I would like to buy this bouquet," I say and point at the tulips.
"That is a really good choice," the clerk says.
He wraps the flowers in some nice paper.
"That will be one hundred and fifty kroner," he says.
I take out my card and pay for the flowers.
"I am going to a dinner tonight," I tell him.
"Then your friend will definitely be happy," he replies.
I take the bouquet and walk out of the shop.
Now I just have to find my bus stop.
